#4471 merged every date report into one known issue. The cause code does not. A report's cause comes from the tenant's locale and booking form, not from the subject line intake merged on.

<Callout kind="warn">
Two causes were filed on one ticket. The table marks the one that has no ticket of its own.
</Callout>

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

`parser` is the shared parser. It reads every date month first, so a day-first tenant's dates come out flipped. `hint` is the other bug: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the field, and the form then reads that field the tenant's way, day first. Reports the desk read as a one-day move stay in the cause the tenant rule filed them under. The table footnotes those.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
